course: dictionary
lesson: 3278
title: Erupt: a sudden burst
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Erupt is a verb, so it shows something that happens. Its forms are erupt, erupts, erupted and erupting. «The volcano began to erupt, throwing out hot ash and rock.» The clues are hot ash and rock, so erupt means to burst out.
explain: Erupt can also mean something starting suddenly and strongly. «The crowd erupted in cheers when the goal went in.» Nobody is throwing out ash here. The cheers are the clue, so erupt means to burst out with sound or feeling.
explain: Erupt has a third meaning too. When a baby's teeth erupt, they push up through the gums. Read the words around erupt, then try each meaning in the sentence. Only one will make sense.
fact: Erupt means to burst out suddenly and strongly.
fact: For a volcano, erupt means to throw out lava, ash, rock and gas.
fact: Eruption is the noun: a sudden, strong burst.
fact: Real volcanoes erupt melted rock pushed by hot gases deep underground, not by vinegar and soda.
fact: Phrases to learn: erupt into, erupt with.
exercise: «Real volcanoes erupt melted rock pushed by hot gases deep underground.» What does erupt mean here? | *To burst out and throw out lava, ash and gas | To fall quietly into the sea | To be painted in bright colours | To shrink and go cold
exercise: «The crowd erupted in cheers.» What does erupted mean? | *To burst out suddenly and strongly | To go to sleep quietly | To walk slowly away | To stay silent and still
exercise: «The science-fair volcano is great fun, but real volcanoes are completely different.» Find and copy the word that means the opposite of pretend. | science | *real | fun | fair
test: Which meaning of erupt fits «Baby Ella's first tooth began to erupt last week.»? | *To push up through the gums | To fall out of the bath | To shine brightly | To burst out lava
test: Which phrase means a sudden, strong start, like a laugh? | sink into mud | rise from bed slowly | fall into sleep | *erupt into laughter
exam: A clarifying question asks about one part you did not understand, such as «What does erupt mean?» Which answer is best? | It means to sleep quietly | It means to be very old | It means to whisper softly | *It means to burst out or start suddenly and strongly
